  "source": "Rishabh Instruments, RISH Master 3430i Operating Manual, DMAN-00IM-0648 Rev D (06/2018)",
  "notes": [
    "Modbus RTU on RS-485, 2400 to 19200 baud selectable on the meter (setup code at holding 18); the manual gives no factory default, so none is set here. Node address 1 to 247.",
    "Measured values are read with function 04 (input area) and settings with function 03 (holding, written with function 16). Each parameter is two registers holding an IEEE 754 float; a read is limited to 20 parameters.",
    "Addresses are the manual's hexadecimal start addresses (30001 is address 0, 40005 is address 4), address base 0.",
    "Normal word order is most significant register first; the meter can be switched to reversed order through the Word order setting (holding 40), which this map does not assume.",
    "Settings marked R/Wp or Wp in the manual are taken to be writable only after the password, if one is set, has been sent; the manual does not define Wp. Setting values are also sent as floats.",
    "The earlier unofficial map listed the measured values as holding registers; the manual says they are 3X registers read with function 04, so they are input registers here.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's manual; not tested on a device."
  ],
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "big",
  "address_base": 0,
  "x_status": "official",
  "revised": "2026-11-16",
  "description": "Touch-screen multifunction meter: phase and average voltages, currents, powers, power factors, angles, frequency, energies, THD, min and max values, plus the setting registers",
  "sources": [
